Subject: Do not clear freed buffers in the HMAC and keygen tests
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted (mhash is unmaintained)

Both tests free tmp and then memset it before assigning a new buffer.
Fil-C stops the program at the write to the freed object. The memset
has no purpose, since tmp is reassigned right after.

--- a/src/hmac_test.c
+++ b/src/hmac_test.c
@@ -76,8 +76,6 @@
 
 	/* Test No 2 */	
 	
-	mutils_memset(tmp, 0, sizeof(tmp));
-	
 	passlen=sizeof(KEY2) - 1;
 	password = (mutils_word8 *) mutils_malloc(passlen+1);
 	mutils_memcpy(password, KEY2, passlen);
--- a/src/keygen_test.c
+++ b/src/keygen_test.c
@@ -121,8 +121,6 @@
 	
 	mhash_keygen_ext(KEYGEN_S2K_SALTED, data, key, keysize, password, passlen);
 
-	mutils_memset(tmp, 0, keysize * 2);
-
 	tmp = mutils_asciify(key, keysize);
 
 	result = mutils_strcmp((mutils_word8 *) KEY2, tmp);
